# The desktop comes up on a bare codex-vm -gop guest and paints its chrome:
# the top bar and its clock, the sidebar buttons, the Shutdown button and
# the Welcome window with its text wrapped (fester, main 12350).
#
# The clock is frozen. The taskbar paints the CMOS RTC, which is host state
# the test cannot twist, and that is what -rtc exists for -- without it this
# frame differs from the recorded one by the digits every single run.
#
# The font row is load-bearing and it reads "CBF bitmap (no TTF on the ESP)":
# no disk is attached, so desk-font's fallback is what is under test here as
# much as the chrome is. A run that ever painted the TTF face would mean the
# harness had grown a medium and this frame no longer says what it says.
vmargs -gop-width 1280 -gop-height 800 -rtc 2026-07-30T06:00:00
boot 4000
settle 2500
